        short = "Modes, flags, mutes",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "A mode is the part of a template for one situation: arenas, raids, duels, or one you switch on yourself. Each mode gets its own tab in the editor." },
            { kind = "code", source = "#WATCH INSTANCE\n#WATCH FLAG\n#WATCH DUEL\n\n#DEFAULT\n/startattack\n\n#MODE ARENA INSTANCE=ARENA\n/use 13\n/startattack\n\n#MODE WPVP FLAG=WPVP\n/use 14\n/startattack\n\n#MODE DUEL DUEL=ANY\n/target DUELOPPONENT\n/startattack\n#IF DUEL=ROGUE\n/use 13\n/startattack" },
            { kind = "try", text = "|cffd0c8b0Try it|r — Preview as |cffa8d8ffFLAG=WPVP|r, then |cffa8d8ffFLAG=WPVP INSTANCE=ARENA|r, then |cffa8d8ffDUEL=ROGUE|r.", example = 1, states = { "FLAG=WPVP", "FLAG=WPVP INSTANCE=ARENA", "DUEL=ROGUE" } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "How a mode works" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffa8d8ff#MODE NAME CONDITION|r starts a mode; it runs until the next |cffa8d8ff#MODE|r. Modes go after |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r and the template's own |cffa8d8ff#IF|rs.", "The lines right after the header are the mode's macro, used while its condition is true.", "An |cffa8d8ff#IF|r inside a mode gets the mode's condition added: above, |cffa8d8ffDUEL=ANY AND DUEL=ROGUE|r.", "A mode with only |cffa8d8ff#IF|rs and none matching falls back to |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r. To make a mode deliberately empty, put |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r right after its header.", "The |cffffd100+ Mode|r button adds |cffa8d8ffRAID|r, |cffa8d8ffDUNGEON|r, |cffa8d8ffBATTLEGROUND|r, |cffa8d8ffARENA|r and |cffa8d8ffDUEL|r modes, a flag mode, or a custom one, with the watch it needs. There is no world mode: the part before the first mode already is the open world.", "|cffa8d8ff#MODE NAME OFF|r parks a mode: it is kept and checked but never used." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Which mode wins" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "A mode's macro beats a template |cffa8d8ff#IF|r with the same number of tests. A more specific |cffa8d8ff#IF|r still wins.", "|cffffd100Duel modes come first, flag modes last.|r While a duel mode is live, other modes are ignored; while any other mode is live, flag modes are ignored. Above, |cffa8d8ffWPVP|r stays on in an arena, but the arena macro is used.", "Two ordinary modes live at once can tie. Give one a priority: |cffa8d8ff#MODE[10] NAME CONDITION|r." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Flags: states you declare" },
            { kind = "para", text = "The game cannot tell world PvP from questing, so you say it yourself. |cffa8d8ffFLAG=WPVP|r is true while the WPVP flag is on." },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Command", "Does" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc flag WPVP|r", "toggles it (put this in a macro on a key)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc flag WPVP on|r", "sets it: |cffa8d8ffon|r, |cffa8d8ffoff|r or |cffa8d8fftoggle|r" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc flag off|r", "switches every flag off" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc flag|r", "lists the flags that are on" },
            } },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "Flag names are up to 5 characters: letters, digits and |cffa8d8ff_|r, not starting with a digit.", "A flag stays on across reloads and logins, per character, until you switch it off.", "The State section and the glowing tube on the left edge of the screen show your flags; click one to toggle it. |cffa8d8ff/qmc tab|r hides the tube.", "Switch flags before a fight: in combat, the change is applied when combat ends." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Mutes: switching a line off" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A mute removes a line from one mode in every template, without editing them. For example, no bombs in duels:" },
            { kind = "code", source = "/qmc mute DUEL Global Thermal Sapper Charge\n/qmc unmute DUEL Global Thermal Sapper Charge\n/qmc mute" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "It matches the line by what it casts or uses, whatever its |cffa8d8ff[conditions]|r: |cffa8d8ffEvasion|r mutes |cffa8d8ff/cast Evasion|r and |cffa8d8ff/cast [nostealth] Evasion|r. Several entries go on one line, separated by |cffa8d8ff;|r.", "A mute never empties a version: if it would remove its last macro line, that version keeps it.", "Mutes are per character and are never exported. |cffa8d8ff/qmc unmute DUEL|r clears a mode's mutes, |cffa8d8ff/qmc unmute|r all of them. The State section lists them, each with an |cffa8d8ffx|r." } },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "compiler",
        title = "Sequences with #STEP",
        short = "Sequences with #STEP",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "A sequence runs the next step on every press, and it keeps working in combat. Game state still picks the version before the fight; the press picks the step." },
            { kind = "code", source = "#SEQUENCE RESET=COMBATSTART,[mod:alt]\n\n#DEFAULT\n#PRE\n/startattack\n#STEP ONCE\n/use 13\n#STEP\n/cast Sinister Strike\n#STEP\n/cast Eviscerate" },
            { kind = "tip", text = "Swap in your own spells. Presses after a reset run: trinket, Sinister Strike, Eviscerate, Sinister Strike, Eviscerate, … |cffa8d8ff/startattack|r runs on every press." },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Block", "Runs" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ff#PRE|r", "every press, before the step" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff#STEP ONCE|r", "once after each reset, as an opener" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff#STEP|r", "in turn, looping" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff#POST|r", "every press, after the step" },
            } },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "Order inside a version: |cffa8d8ff#PRE|r, then |cffa8d8ff#STEP ONCE|r steps, then |cffa8d8ff#STEP|r steps, then |cffa8d8ff#POST|r. Every line must be under one of them.", "Any version can be a sequence: |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r, an |cffa8d8ff#IF|r, a mode. Others in the same template can stay plain.", "Unlike |cffa8d8ff/castsequence|r, a step is used up even when its cast fails, so the sequence never gets stuck on one spell." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Starting over" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A sequence goes back to its first step when the template recompiles, and when combat ends. |cffa8d8ff#SEQUENCE RESET=|r adds more:" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Reset", "Starts over when" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffCOMBATSTART|r", "combat starts, so every fight begins with the openers" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffNOTARGET|r", "you have no target, or it is dead" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff[mod:alt]|r", "you press it with these conditions true" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffNOCOMBAT|r", "turns off the reset at the end of combat" },
            } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Every sequence also gets a reset button: |cffa8d8ff/click WMC_<name>_RESET|r, usable in combat. There is no reset on switching targets or after a pause; the game gives addons no way to see either during combat." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "The global cooldown" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Every press is one step, even during the global cooldown. Spamming the key skips steps, and a skipped opener only comes back after a reset. Keep sequences short and use |cffa8d8ffCOMBATSTART|r or a reset key." },
            { kind = "try", text = "|cffd0c8b0Try it|r — the Forms panel notes how many steps |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r has and which resets are in effect, ending with the reset button's |cffa8d8ff/click|r line.", example = 1, states = {  } },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "compiler",
        title = "Your group: placeholders and pins",
        short = "Your group, pins",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "Outside an arena, class placeholders point at your own party or raid: |cffa8d8ff[@PRIEST]|r is a priest in your group. They work anywhere you have a group: the open world, battlegrounds, dungeons and raids, in any mode." },
            { kind = "code", source = "#WATCH GROUP\n#WATCH FLAG\n\n#DEFAULT\n/startattack\n\n#MODE WPVP FLAG=WPVP\n/cast [@ANY,help] Hand of Freedom" },
            { kind = "tip", text = "In world PvP, cast on the healer you pinned with |cffa8d8ff/qmc pin ANY|r. Swap in a spell of your own." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "The placeholders" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Write", "Becomes" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffPRIEST|r, |cffa8d8ffPRIEST#2|r", "the first, or second, priest in the group (never you)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffPRIESTPET|r", "that priest's pet" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffMAINTANK|r, |cffa8d8ffMAINASSIST|r", "the raid's assigned main tank or main assist (can be you)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffANY|r", "the member you pinned with |cffa8d8ff/qmc pin ANY|r" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffTASK|r", "the member another addon pinned (page 12)" },
            } },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "Use them as |cffa8d8ff[@PRIEST]|r, or bare and in capitals: |cffa8d8ff/target PRIEST|r.", "Order is raid order, or party order in a party. Offline members are skipped.", "They become the player's name, so a raid member moving groups does not break the macro.", "They point at your group only. In world PvP, |cffa8d8ff[@ROGUE]|r is a rogue on your side, never an enemy: enemies are only reachable by class in arenas (page 4).", "Solo, nothing resolves and the line does nothing. |cffa8d8ffMAINTANK|r and |cffa8d8ffMAINASSIST|r need a raid, since parties have no assignments.", "Templates using them need |cffa8d8ff#WATCH GROUP|r; the editor adds it." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Pins: choosing who a placeholder means" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Command", "Does" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc pin MAGE|r", "your target becomes |cffa8d8ffMAGE|r; other mages follow as |cffa8d8ffMAGE#2|r, …" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc pin MAGE Name|r", "pins that member by name" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc pin ANY|r", "your target becomes |cffa8d8ffANY|r, whatever their class" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc unpin MAGE|r", "clears one pin; |cffa8d8ff/qmc unpin|r clears all" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc pin|r", "lists the pins" },
            } },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "A pinned player who leaves or goes offline is skipped, and used again when they return.", "Pins last until you leave the group, log out or reload.", "|cffa8d8ffANY|r has no fallback: unpinned, the line does nothing. It also works in arenas, for your partner; class pins do not, since class placeholders mean opponents there.", "The State section and the screen-edge tube list your pins, each with an |cffa8d8ffx|r." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Buffs on your group" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Placeholders also work in aura conditions, including time left:" },
            { kind = "code", source = "#WATCH AURA\n#WATCH GROUP\n\n#DEFAULT\n\n#IF NOT AURA:ANY=\"POWER WORD: FORTITUDE\" OR AURA:ANY:\"POWER WORD: FORTITUDE\".TIME<2m\n/cast [@ANY] Power Word: Fortitude" },
            { kind = "try", text = "|cffd0c8b0Try it|r — Preview as |cffa8d8ffAURA:ANY:\"POWER WORD: FORTITUDE\".TIME=1m|r. The preview cannot fake a group, so |cffa8d8ff@ANY|r itself only resolves with a real pin.", example = 2, states = { "AURA:ANY:\"POWER WORD: FORTITUDE\".TIME=1m" } },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "compiler",
        title = "A warlock's succubus in duels",
        short = "Succubus in duels",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "In a duel against a warlock, |cffa8d8ffSUCCUBUS|r in your macro becomes the name of their succubus, so any class can target, interrupt or crowd-control it: Kick, Counterspell, Wind Shear, Pummel, Mind Freeze, Polymorph, Fear, Hex, Repentance, Cyclone." },
            { kind = "code", source = "#WATCH DUEL\n\n#DEFAULT\n/startattack\n\n#IF DUEL_SUCCUBUS=YES\n/target SUCCUBUS\n/focus\n/targetlasttarget\n/cast [@focus] Shadowstep\n/cast [@focus] Kick" },
            { kind = "tip", text = "Swap in your own interrupt or crowd control." },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffffd100How the name is learned.|r The game shows another player's pet name nowhere except the combat log. The first time their succubus casts Seduction on you in a duel, Quintessence learns its name and remembers it for that warlock.", "|cffffd100Next time.|r When you duel the same warlock again, the name is ready from the challenge, before the countdown ends.", "|cffa8d8ffDUEL_SUCCUBUS=YES|r is true while a name is known. Use it, as above, so the version only appears once there is a succubus to target.", "Write |cffa8d8ffSUCCUBUS|r in capitals and without |cffa8d8ff@|r: |cffa8d8ff/target SUCCUBUS|r, |cffa8d8ff/focus SUCCUBUS|r. With no name known it becomes |cffa8d8ffarena0|r and does nothing." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Managing the names" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Command", "Does" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc duel add Warlock Petname|r", "stores a name you learned elsewhere" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc duel list|r", "shows stored names (|cffa8d8ff/qmc duel list text|r filters)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc duel forget Warlock|r", "removes one" },
            } },
            { kind = "try", text = "|cffd0c8b0Try it|r — Preview as |cffa8d8ffDUEL=WARLOCK DUEL_SUCCUBUS=YES|r.", example = 1, states = { "DUEL=WARLOCK DUEL_SUCCUBUS=YES" } },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "compiler",
        title = "Reading the editor",
        short = "Reading the editor",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "The editor shows what the button holds, why that version was picked, and what Quintessence knows about the game. Most questions about a template are answered by the Forms panel." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Preview as" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Type a situation to see what the template would do in it, without being there:" },
            { kind = "code", source = "INSTANCE=ARENA ARENA1=MAGE ARENA2=ROGUE FLAG=WPVP" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffa8d8ffFIELD=VALUE|r terms separated by spaces. No |cffa8d8ffOR|r, |cffa8d8ffNOT|r or declared names.", "Arena slots, duels, flags, auras (with |cffa8d8ff.TIME|r and |cffa8d8ff.STACKS|r) and cooldowns can all be faked. Your group cannot: placeholders keep using your real group.", "On a mode's tab, |cffffd100This mode|r fills in the mode's condition; |cffffd100Live|r clears the line.", "Only the editor is affected. Your buttons keep following the real game, and the line is cleared when you close the window." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Button" },
            { kind = "para", text = "One line: the version the button holds (|cffa8d8ffDEFAULT|r, |cffa8d8ffIF #3|r), whether it is up to date or waiting for combat to end, and its size. A macro over the game's length limit is split across several buttons automatically; the line says \"chained across N buttons\"." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Forms" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Warnings first, then one row per version: its line, its priority, a result and its condition. Hover a condition for the full text and the reason." },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Result", "Means" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffselected|r", "this version is in use" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffmatched|r", "true, but another version has more tests or a higher priority" },
                { "|cffa8d8fftie|r", "true with the same tests and priority as another: an error to fix" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffyields|r", "its mode gives way to a duel mode, or a flag mode to another mode (page 7)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffno|r", "its condition is false" },
            } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "State" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Your flags (click to toggle), pins and mutes, then what Quintessence knows right now: target, you, zone, arena, party, duel and group. A row with nothing to show is hidden." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Errors and warnings" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "An |cffffd100error|r turns its line and its tab red, and the button keeps its last good macro. Common ones: a missing |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r, a misspelled field, a |cffa8d8ff#DECLARE|r after |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r, a missing |cffa8d8ff#ENDIF|r, and a tie.", "A |cffffd100warning|r never stops a template. It flags a value that can never match (|cffa8d8ffCLASS=MAGEE|r), or a missing watch, so the version would only update on login or save." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Comments" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A line starting with |cffa8d8ff#--|r is a note for yourself. It never reaches the macro and costs no characters:" },
            { kind = "code", source = "#-- Trinket first; add the interrupt once it's bound\n#DEFAULT\n/use 13" },
            { kind = "para", text = "There are no comments at the end of a line: |cffa8d8ff/cast Kick #-- note|r is macro text." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Sharing templates" },
            { kind = "para", text = "|cffffd100Export|r gives a template as readable text, and |cffffd100Export All|r every template of the class shown. |cffffd100Import|r takes any number of them; a name already in use gets a free one (|cffa8d8ffname_2|r). Categories, flags, pins and mutes are not exported." },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "compiler",
        title = "Commands and other addons",
        short = "Commands, addons",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "Every command also works as |cffa8d8ff/wmc|r." },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Command", "Does" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc|r", "opens or closes the window" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc guide [page]|r", "opens or closes this guide, at a page if given (also the book icon at the right of the editor's heading)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc flag NAME [on||off||toggle]|r", "switches a flag; |cffa8d8ff/qmc flag off|r all off; |cffa8d8ff/qmc flag|r lists them (page 7)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc pin CLASS||ANY [Name]|r", "pins your target, or a named member; |cffa8d8ff/qmc pin|r lists pins (page 9)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc unpin [CLASS||ANY]|r", "clears one pin, or all" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc mute MODE line[; line]|r", "mutes lines in a mode; |cffa8d8ff/qmc mute|r lists mutes (page 7)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc unmute [MODE [line]]|r", "unmutes a line, a mode, or everything" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc duel add||list||forget|r", "manages stored succubus names (page 10)" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc minimap|r", "hides or shows the minimap button" },
                { "|cffa8d8ff/qmc tab|r", "hides or shows the flag tube on the screen edge" },
            } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Buttons to |cffa8d8ff/click|r from your own macros:" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffa8d8ff/click WMC_<name>|r — the template.", "|cffa8d8ff/click WMC_<name>_RESET|r — restarts a sequence, also in combat (page 8)." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "For other addons" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A WeakAura or a raid addon can switch your flags and set pins through |cffa8d8ffWMacroCompiler.API|r, for example to turn a boss branch on before the pull and point |cffa8d8ffTASK|r at the player you were assigned:" },
            { kind = "code", source = "#WATCH FLAG\n#WATCH GROUP\n\n#DEFAULT\n/cast Divine Shield\n\n#IF FLAG=LK\n/cast [@TASK] Hand of Protection" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Function", "Does" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffSetFlag(name, on)|r", "like |cffa8d8ff/qmc flag|r; |cffa8d8ffon|r = true, false, or nil to toggle" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffGetFlag(name)|r", "true or false" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffSetPin(slot, player)|r", "like |cffa8d8ff/qmc pin|r; |cffa8d8ffslot|r = |cffa8d8ffTASK|r, |cffa8d8ffANY|r or a class" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffClearPin(slot)|r, |cffa8d8ffGetPin(slot)|r", "like |cffa8d8ff/qmc unpin|r; the pinned name" },
            } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Every change made this way is announced in chat as \"(set by another addon)\". As with the commands, a change made in combat reaches the button when combat ends, so set things up before the pull." },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "compiler",
        title = "Field cheat sheet",
        short = "Field cheat sheet",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "Every condition field, with its values and the |cffa8d8ff#WATCH|r it needs. Values are case-insensitive; quote names with spaces." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "You, your target and where you are" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Field", "Values", "Watch", "Page" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffPLAYER_CLASS|r", "a class", "none", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffPLAYER_SPEC|r", "a spec", "|cffa8d8ffPLAYER_SPEC|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffCLASS|r", "the target's class", "|cffa8d8ffCLASS|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffSPEC|r", "the target's spec", "|cffa8d8ffSPEC|r", "4" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffNAME|r", "the target's name", "|cffa8d8ffNAME|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffREACTION|r", "|cffa8d8ffENEMY|r, |cffa8d8ffALLY|r, |cffa8d8ffNEUTRAL|r", "|cffa8d8ffREACTION|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffINSTANCE|r", "|cffa8d8ffNONE|r, |cffa8d8ffPARTY|r, |cffa8d8ffRAID|r, |cffa8d8ffPVP|r, |cffa8d8ffARENA|r", "|cffa8d8ffINSTANCE|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffINSTANCE_NAME|r", "the instance's name", "|cffa8d8ffINSTANCE|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffZONE|r", "the zone's name", "|cffa8d8ffZONE|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffPLAYER_CD|r (or |cffa8d8ffPCD|r)", "a spell or item on cooldown", "|cffa8d8ffPLAYER_CD|r", "5" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffPET|r", "|cffa8d8ffYES|r, |cffa8d8ffNO|r, |cffa8d8ffIMP|r, |cffa8d8ffSUCCUBUS|r, |cffa8d8ffFELHUNTER|r, |cffa8d8ffVOIDWALKER|r, |cffa8d8ffFELGUARD|r, |cffa8d8ffINFERNAL|r", "|cffa8d8ffPET|r", "5" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffFLAG|r", "a flag name, up to 5 characters", "|cffa8d8ffFLAG|r", "7" },
            } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Arenas, party and duels" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Field", "Values", "Watch", "Page" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffARENA1|r–|cffa8d8ffARENA5|r", "the class in that enemy slot", "|cffa8d8ffARENA|r", "4" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffCOMP|r", "a class on the enemy team", "|cffa8d8ffARENA|r", "4" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffPARTY1|r–|cffa8d8ffPARTY4|r", "a party member's class", "|cffa8d8ffPARTY|r", "2" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffDUEL|r", "the opponent's class, or |cffa8d8ffANY|r", "|cffa8d8ffDUEL|r", "4" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffDUEL_SUCCUBUS|r", "|cffa8d8ffYES|r, |cffa8d8ffNO|r", "|cffa8d8ffDUEL|r", "10" },
            } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Fields with a unit" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Field", "Values", "Watch", "Page" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffAURA:<unit>|r", "an aura name", "|cffa8d8ffAURA|r", "5" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffAURA:<unit>:\"name\".TIME|r", "|cffa8d8ff<|r, |cffa8d8ff<=|r, |cffa8d8ff>|r, |cffa8d8ff>=|r and |cffa8d8ff90s|r, |cffa8d8ff15m|r, |cffa8d8ff1h|r (|cffa8d8ffSELF|r and group placeholders only)", "|cffa8d8ffAURA|r", "5" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffAURA:<unit>:\"name\".STACKS|r", "|cffa8d8ff<|r, |cffa8d8ff<=|r, |cffa8d8ff>|r, |cffa8d8ff>=|r and a number (same units)", "|cffa8d8ffAURA|r", "5" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffCOMBAT:<unit>|r", "|cffa8d8ffYES|r, |cffa8d8ffNO|r", "|cffa8d8ffCOMBAT|r", "5" },
            } },
            { kind = "para", text = "The units each field accepts are in the table on page 5. A |cffa8d8ffCOMP:|r unit also needs |cffa8d8ff#WATCH ARENA|r, and a group placeholder unit |cffa8d8ff#WATCH GROUP|r." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Values" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffffd100Classes:|r |cffa8d8ffDEATHKNIGHT|r, |cffa8d8ffDRUID|r, |cffa8d8ffHUNTER|r, |cffa8d8ffMAGE|r, |cffa8d8ffPALADIN|r, |cffa8d8ffPRIEST|r, |cffa8d8ffROGUE|r, |cffa8d8ffSHAMAN|r, |cffa8d8ffWARLOCK|r, |cffa8d8ffWARRIOR|r.", "|cffffd100Specs:|r |cffa8d8ffBLOOD|r, |cffa8d8ffFROST|r, |cffa8d8ffUNHOLY|r · |cffa8d8ffBALANCE|r, |cffa8d8ffFERAL|r, |cffa8d8ffRESTORATION|r · |cffa8d8ffBEAST_MASTERY|r, |cffa8d8ffMARKSMANSHIP|r, |cffa8d8ffSURVIVAL|r · |cffa8d8ffARCANE|r, |cffa8d8ffFIRE|r, |cffa8d8ffFROST|r · |cffa8d8ffHOLY|r, |cffa8d8ffPROTECTION|r, |cffa8d8ffRETRIBUTION|r · |cffa8d8ffDISCIPLINE|r, |cffa8d8ffHOLY|r, |cffa8d8ffSHADOW|r · |cffa8d8ffASSASSINATION|r, |cffa8d8ffCOMBAT|r, |cffa8d8ffSUBTLETY|r · |cffa8d8ffELEMENTAL|r, |cffa8d8ffENHANCEMENT|r, |cffa8d8ffRESTORATION|r · |cffa8d8ffAFFLICTION|r, |cffa8d8ffDEMONOLOGY|r, |cffa8d8ffDESTRUCTION|r · |cffa8d8ffARMS|r, |cffa8d8ffFURY|r, |cffa8d8ffPROTECTION|r.", "|cffffd100Joining tests:|r |cffa8d8ffAND|r, |cffa8d8ffOR|r, |cffa8d8ffNOT|r, |cffa8d8ff[A,B,C]|r lists (one test each), |cffa8d8ff#DECLARE|r names (one test each)." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Placeholders in macro text" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Write", "Becomes", "Page" }, rows = {
                { "|cffa8d8ffROGUE|r, |cffa8d8ffROGUE#2|r, |cffa8d8ffROGUEPET|r", "in an arena: that enemy; elsewhere: that group member", "4, 9" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffNOTROGUE|r", "the first enemy known not to be a rogue (arenas only)", "4" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffMAINTANK|r, |cffa8d8ffMAINASSIST|r", "the raid's assignment", "9" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffANY|r, |cffa8d8ffTASK|r", "the member pinned by you, or by another addon", "9, 12" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffDUELOPPONENT|r", "your duel opponent's name", "4" },
                { "|cffa8d8ffSUCCUBUS|r", "your duel opponent's succubus", "10" },
            } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Use |cffa8d8ff[@ROGUE]|r, or the bare word in capitals: |cffa8d8ff/target ROGUE|r. |cffa8d8ffSUCCUBUS|r has only the bare form." },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "macros",
        title = "The macro window",
        short = "The macro window",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "|cffa8d8ff/qmb|r opens Quintessence Macros, in place of Blizzard's macro window: |cffa8d8ff/macro|r, the Esc menu's Macros button and its key binding open it too. |cffa8d8ff/qmb blizzard|r still opens Blizzard's." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Your macro slots" },
            { kind = "para", text = "The General and Character slots sit side by side at the top, each with its count. Click a macro to edit it, or a free slot to start a new macro there. Drag a macro onto an action bar as usual. |cffffd100New|r makes a macro in the lit tab, the one you last clicked in." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Editing" },
            { kind = "para", text = "The editor below works as Blizzard's: the icon (click it to pick another), the name, the text, |cffffd100Save|r and |cffffd100Revert|r. The text is coloured as in the Compiler's editor, and the line under it counts its characters." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Long macros" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A macro may be longer than the game's 255 characters. Past that, its slot holds |cffa8d8ff/click QMB|r and a number, and a hidden button runs the whole text. If the text starts with |cffa8d8ff#showtooltip|r, that line is kept in the slot so the icon still follows it. Like a template, a long macro changes only out of combat." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Templates from macros" },
            { kind = "para", text = "|cffffd100Template|r turns the macro into a Compiler template of the same name, the macro's text as its |cffa8d8ff#DEFAULT|r. |cffffd100Switch|r also makes the macro click the template's button, so it keeps its place on your bars; |cffffd100Make|r leaves the macro as it was." },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "macros",
        title = "The bank",
        short = "The bank",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "The column on the right is the bank: every macro you keep, in as many categories as you like, account-wide. Like the Compiler's class list, it has a |cffffd100General|r section and one per class. Pick one in |cffffd100Bank section|r (the window opens on your class), or find a macro with |cffffd100Search|r: by name, or, with the button at its end showing a page, in the text too (the Compiler's Search does the same for templates). A macro shown in white is in one of this character's slots." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Saving and loading" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffffd100Bank|r saves the macro in the editor to the bank. From then on the slot and the bank macro are linked: |cffffd100Save|r updates both, and every other slot that holds it. |cffffd100Bank|r's list checks the categories that already hold the macro; picking another one saves a copy there. When the tab is loaded from that category, the copy takes over: |cffffd100Save|r edits it, and the macro's key runs it.", "|cffffd100Load|r puts the selected bank macro into the lit tab. Shift-|cffffd100Load|r, or a category's right-click menu, loads its whole category.", "Right-click a macro or a category for the rest: move, rename, delete, or save a whole tab's macros into a category." } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Deleting a macro from the bank never takes it out of a slot. A macro that has to leave a slot and isn't in the bank yet is saved to its section's |cffffd100Unsorted|r first, so nothing is lost." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Settings" },
            { kind = "para", text = "The gear by |cffffd100Bank section|r opens the bank's settings:" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffffd100Save new macros to the bank|r: a macro made here, or with the Compiler's |cffffd100Make Macro|r, goes into the category its tab was loaded from.", "|cffffd100Import from MacroBank|r, while MacroBank is enabled: copies its macros and categories (also |cffa8d8ff/qmb import|r).", "Whether |cffa8d8ff/macro|r opens this window or Blizzard's (also |cffa8d8ff/qmb takeover on|r or |cffa8d8ffoff|r)." } },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "macros",
        title = "Loadouts",
        short = "Loadouts",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "A loadout is a named set of bank categories for each tab. Applying it makes the tabs hold exactly those categories' macros. Your bank can keep far more macros than the game's slots, so each loadout picks which categories are in them: one for PvP and another for PvE, for example, or a class's own macros in the 36 General slots, making the General tab class-specific. |cffffd100Give each class its own General tab|r, in the bank's settings, does this by default." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Making one" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = true, items = { "Load the categories you want into each tab.", "Open |cffffd100Settings|r by the |cffffd100Loadout|r field and choose |cffffd100New|r: the loadout takes the categories the tabs were last loaded from.", "Add or remove categories there at any time." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Shared and per character" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A loadout belongs to a class: every character of that class sees the same loadouts, and only those. Part of it is the class's; the rest each character keeps for itself." },
            { kind = "para", text = "The class shares:" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "The loadout itself: its name and its categories for each tab. Adding a category, renaming the loadout or deleting it does so for every character of the class.", "The talent rules (|cffffd100A spec...|r, |cffffd100A talent...|r), so a new character picks its loadout by its talents with nothing to set up.", "The macros: the bank and the 36 General slots are account-wide, which is why each apply fills the General tab again." } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Each character keeps:" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "|cffffd100Use it|r: its loadout for login, for primary talents and for secondary talents.", "The loadout it has in use. When several fit its talents, the one it applied last wins.", "Its action bars for each loadout, per talent group (page 17).", "Its gear set for each loadout, per spec (page 17)." } },
            { kind = "para", text = "Deleting a loadout also deletes every character's bars and gear sets for it." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Which loadout is used" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Pick one in the |cffffd100Loadout|r field and press |cffffd100Apply|r, or type |cffa8d8ff/qmb load|r and its name. Otherwise Quintessence chooses, at login and whenever your talents change:" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = true, items = { "Your talents. A rule is a spec (|cffffd100A spec...|r: one of the class's three trees), a talent (|cffffd100A talent...|r: one with points), or both. Rules count for every character of the class, and the first that fits wins.", "Otherwise the talent group: the loadout you chose for |cffffd100primary|r or |cffffd100secondary|r talents.", "Otherwise the loadout chosen for |cffffd100login|r." } },
            { kind = "para", text = "While you spend points nothing happens; the loadout changes once the talents settle. In combat it waits until the fight ends. |cffffd100Give each class its own General tab|r, in the bank's settings, gives a class without loadouts one of its own, so its characters stop sharing what the last character left in General." },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "macros",
        title = "Bars and gear",
        short = "Bars and gear",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "Applying a loadout replaces your macros, and the game empties every button that held a macro that went away. So each loadout remembers your whole action bars, per talent group, and puts them back when it is applied: its macros, other macros, spells, items, equipment sets and companions." },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "The bars are remembered as you leave them: move a button, and the loadout keeps it there.", "Putting them back only fills empty buttons; it never covers a spell or item you have put there since.", "Something that can't be placed yet, a spell not learned or an item not in your bags, waits: its button stays empty and fills in by itself once you learn the spell or get the item." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "A new character" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A character applying a loadout for the first time starts from the bars of another of its class: one at the highest level first, then the same race, then the same realm. Another race's racials are left empty." },
            { kind = "para", text = "Putting the bars back and starting from another character's can each be switched off in the bank's settings. |cffa8d8ff/qmb bars|r says what the bank sees on your bars." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Gear sets" },
            { kind = "para", text = "A loadout also puts on an equipment set from the game's Equipment Manager, one for each spec. Under one loadout, Subtlety can wear your PvP set and Combat another, whichever talent group each spec is in." },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "The first set you put on in a spec, with the loadout in use, is kept for that spec: from the character window, with |cffa8d8ff/equipset|r, or from an action bar button.", "Later swaps don't change it, so a fishing set stays a fishing set. To change it, use |cffffd100A spec's set...|r in the loadout's settings, or clear it with the X and put the new one on.", "The set goes on when the loadout is applied, and when your talents change to another spec that keeps the loadout. In combat it waits until the fight ends.", "Equipment sets are each character's own in the game, so each character keeps its own for each loadout. A spec with none leaves your gear as it is." } },
        },
    },
    {
        part = "macros",
        title = "Key bindings",
        short = "Key bindings",
        blocks = {
            { kind = "para", text = "A key can run a template or a bank macro directly: no macro, no slot and no action bar button." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Setting a key" },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "In the Compiler: the keycap in the template source box's corner, or right-click the template in the list.", "In Quintessence Macros: the keycap in a bank macro's editor, or |cffffd100Key binding...|r in its right-click menu. The macro has to be in the bank.", "Then press the key. Shift, Ctrl and Alt combinations work, and so do mouse buttons 3 to 5 and the wheel. The key is set at once; |cffffd100Clear|r removes it." } },
            { kind = "para", text = "The Compiler's template list shows each key at the end of its row, shortened: |cffa8d8ffc-F|r is Ctrl-F, |cffa8d8ffs-M4|r is Shift and mouse button 4." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Where a key applies" },
            { kind = "para", text = "The boxes in the key popup choose where the key applies. Without them, it follows where the template or macro lives:" },
            { kind = "table", header = { "Box", "The key applies on", "Without the box" }, rows = {
                { "(none)", "every character", "a GENERAL template or bank macro" },
                { "|cffffd100Rogue only|r", "every character of the class", "a class template or bank macro" },
                { "|cffffd100Subtlety only|r", "the class, in that spec", "(none)" },
            } },
            { kind = "para", text = "On one key, the most specific wins: your spec's, then your class's, then everyone's. So a hunter can keep Ctrl-F for one template while your rogue uses it for another. A spec's key follows your spec as gear sets do, when you respec or switch talent groups." },
            { kind = "para", text = "A template or macro has one key on each level; setting a new one replaces it." },
            { kind = "heading", text = "Your own bindings" },
            { kind = "para", text = "Quintessence's keys sit over the game's key bindings without changing them. The popup tells you when a key was in use (\"It overrides your binding: Action Button 3\"), and your binding comes back when you clear the key. The game's Key Bindings window doesn't show Quintessence's keys; the list below does." },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "A key fires as you press it down.", "A key set during combat takes effect when the fight ends.", "Keys aren't part of loadouts: a template already changes with the situation, and a bank macro on a key needs no macro slot." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "The list" },
            { kind = "para", text = "|cffffd100Key Bindings|r shows every key that can apply on this character, templates first, then macros. Open it from the list icon on the Compiler's rail or on the flyout, |cffffd100Key bindings...|r in the bank's settings, or |cffa8d8ff/qmb keys|r." },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "Under each key: its level, and what it is doing here: \"not this spec\", \"replaced by Subtlety's\", \"over Action Button 5\".", "A dim key doesn't apply right now. A red one belongs to a disabled template, or to a template or macro that is gone.", "Click a row to change its key; the X removes it." } },
            { kind = "heading", text = "From BindPad" },
            { kind = "para", text = "While BindPad is enabled, Quintessence offers once to bring its keys over; later, |cffffd100Import from BindPad|r in the bank's settings, or |cffa8d8ff/qmb keys import|r." },
            { kind = "list", ordered = false, items = { "BindPad's own macros become bank macros, in your class's |cffffd100Unsorted|r (those on BindPad's General tab in General's), each with its key.", "A key on one of your macros goes to the bank macro with the same name and text, if there is one.", "A key BindPad had in both talent groups goes on your class; in one group only, on that group's spec.", "Spells and items stay with BindPad, or the game's Key Bindings window: the chat lists them.", "A key you already gave something in Quintessence keeps it." } },
        },
    },
}
